  <amendment date="2026-07-18" by="spaarkeai-compose-r3 re-architecture">
    SERVER-ONLY scope now. This task verifies-and-wires `DocxAnnotationWriter` so AI redlines/comments
    compose correctly onto the SERVER-AUTHORED baseline — both the retained-original delta (022 synthesizer)
    AND the from-scratch render (026 `ComposeDocumentRenderer`). The CLIENT reject-baseline rewire (retiring
    `ComposeEditor.serializeForSave` / `buildRejectBaselineJson` / `tipTapJsonToDocxBytes`) is MOVED to task
    027 (client content-model cutover) — do NOT do client work here. Baseline note: the annotation-apply
    seam is now `ComposeService.SaveAsync` (post-Increment-A, `ce50c9877`), where `request.Annotations` are
    applied via `_annotationWriter.Annotate` AFTER the synthesizer/renderer produces `contentToPersist` — so
    the annotations decorate a FAITHFUL baseline, not a reconstruction. Add unit tests proving AI redline +
    direct-typing delta (and AI redline + rendered born-in-editor doc) compose without corrupting either set.
  </amendment>

  <prompt>
    Implement FR-04: AI redlines + comments continue to apply via the EXISTING `DocxAnnotationWriter`
    (native `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment`) — unchanged from R2 — but now onto the retained-original
    baseline established by the E1 cutover (task 022), NOT onto a TipTap reconstruction. This is a
    VERIFY-AND-WIRE task, not a new component: reuse `DocxAnnotationWriter.cs` verbatim and confirm the
    annotation pass runs on the resolved retained-original baseline inside the inverted `SaveAsync`
    flow, composing correctly with the direct-typing splice+comparer delta (020/021). Prove an accepted
    AI redline persists as native OOXML on the faithful baseline.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET 8 developer familiar with the R2 Compose annotation pipeline (`DocxAnnotationWriter`
    `Annotate`, `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment`) and the inverted `SaveAsync` flow from task 022.
    Comfortable verifying composition order between the direct-typing delta and the AI-annotation pass.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Confirmed + tested wiring so that AI redlines/comments apply via the unchanged `DocxAnnotationWriter`
    onto the retained-original baseline (post-022), producing native `w:ins`/`w:del`/`w:comment` on the
    faithful document. Matching unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Services/Compose/` assert an
    accepted AI redline persists as native OOXML on the retained-original baseline and composes with the
    direct-typing delta without corrupting either.</goal>

